🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
In this PR #101554, a privateuse1Stubs register has been added, which allows third-party devices to register a ProfilerStubs to enable the emit functionality. We need to support the emit functionality for third-party devices in the profiler_kineto.cpp::enableProfiler(...) function. The following modifications are required:

Add PRIVATEUSE1 to the ProfilerState and ActiveProfilerType structures
Add privateuse1_observer.h and privateuse1_observer.cpp in the torch/csrc/profiler/standalone directory. The main logic is to add a pushPRIVATEUSE1CallbacksStub registrar, which can be used to register pushXXXCallbacks of third-party devices.

My code snippet
torch/csrc/autograd/profiler_kineto.cpp
void enableProfiler(
    const torch::profiler::impl::ProfilerConfig& config,
    const std::set<torch::profiler::impl::ActivityType>& activities,
    const std::unordered_set<at::RecordScope>& scopes) {
  const auto has_cpu = activities.count(ActivityType::CPU);
  TORCH_CHECK(
      KinetoThreadLocalState::get(/*global=*/config.global()) == nullptr,
      "Profiler is already enabled",
      (config.global() ? "." : " on this thread."));

  if (config.state == ProfilerState::NVTX) {
    torch::profiler::impl::pushNVTXCallbacks(config, scopes);
    return;
  } else if (config.state == ProfilerState::ITT) {
    torch::profiler::impl::pushITTCallbacks(config, scopes);
    return;
  } else if (config.state == ProfilerState::PRIVATEUSE1) {
    torch::profiler::impl::pushPRIVATEUSE1CallbacksStub(
        c10::kPrivateUse1, config, scopes);
    return;
  }
